## 🚀 Session bootstrap (read this first, every session)

These documents are **not** auto-loaded each turn — only this router is. So:

- **New session** (you have *not* yet loaded the boot set this session) → run
  **`/start-session`**. If the user dives straight into work without it, first read
  the **boot set** yourself, then continue:
  `documentation/CONSTITUTION.md`, `documentation/IDENTITY.md`,
  `documentation/SOUL.md`, `documentation/WORKFLOW.md`, `documentation/ROLES.md`,
  `documentation/NEXT_SESSION.md`, and load `documentation/MEMORY.md`
  (+ connect the vector DB if configured). **Never skip `NEXT_SESSION.md`** — it
  tells you where the last session left off and what to do next.
- **Mid-session** (the boot set is already in your context) → **do not re-read.**
  You already have the context; just keep working.
- **On demand only** (read when a task needs them, not at startup):
  `documentation/INITIALIZATION.md`, `documentation/CHANGELOG.md`,
  `documentation/STRUCTURE.json`, `documentation/configuration.json`,
  `documentation/playbooks/*`.
- **Session end** → run **`/finalize-session`** to soft-shutdown: reflect, update
  the living docs, rewrite `NEXT_SESSION.md`, re-condense `CHANGELOG.md`, run `doctor`.

